	(text "PWR_FLAG: these rails reach their loads only through passive parts (the edge fingers, USB-C, the P-FET, the SS34)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 96.52 175.26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1e7fa103-559d-5395-8d30-d78f9a39283c")
	)
	(text "Power tree: +5V is the OR of the console's 5 V and USB VBUS (FujiNet-NES Rev0's circuit).\n  CONS_5V  edge 15, the console's 7805, through Q1 AO3401A (D = CONS_5V, S = +5V, G = VBUS): fully on (~30 mV)\n           with no USB; off with VBUS present, when only its body diode is left, which never passes anything\n           back into the console.\n  VBUS     the ESP32-S3 board (fujiversal-studio2, the USB host, on its own supply), through D5 SS34: with it\n           connected the cart takes nothing from the console's 7805.  R27 4.7k holds VBUS (the P-FET's gate)\n           low with no cable and against the SS34's reverse leakage.\n+5V feeds the 74HCT541 / '32 / '1G02 / '14 and U6 AP2112K -> +3V3 (every RP2354B supply pin: it rises with +5V, so the\n5 V-tolerant pads are never unpowered with 5 V on them).  The cart draws ~50 mA; nothing else is on this board.\nUSB-C: the RP2354B native USB to the S3 board (UFP, 5.1k Rd); ESD on D+, D- and VBUS.  TP13, TP14, TP15 and TP16 are\nbring-up pads."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 96.52 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d3e17361-8add-584a-8080-81717d3a0317")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
